Koel Pharma Ltd, an imagined company, was registered with an authorised capital of 2,00,000 equity shares of ₹10 each. In its first year it:

1. issued 10,000 shares as fully paid to its promoters for their services in forming the company;
2. bought plant for ₹3,60,000 from Rawat Engineering and paid by issuing equity shares at a premium of ₹2 per share;
3. offered 1,00,000 shares to the public at par, payable ₹4 on application and ₹6 on allotment. All the shares were applied for and allotted; Karan, holding 2,000 shares, did not pay the allotment money. The company keeps a Calls in Arrears Account.

Pass the journal entries and prepare the notes to accounts on Share Capital and on Reserves and Surplus.
